 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It' not random, it's German grammar. In German, nouns have gender, and that affects the way we use words. Yes, it is. Each gender has its own set of gender specific words. For example, a chair is male, a table is female, and a door is neuter. It may seem bizarre at first, but it' actually quite useful. Many common words have feminine, masculine, or neuter gender. Then congrats, you've unlocked one of the smaller keys to speaking German. Sorry, I was caught up with something else. In German, you say em empty or em kochen?",
